    <string name="holdem_help_title">How to play Texas Hold\'em</string>
    <string name="holdem_help_text">Play for chips only: there is no real money. Everyone starts with the same stack, and the last player holding chips wins.\n\nEach hand you get two private cards. Five shared cards come face up on the table: three (the flop), then one (the turn), then one (the river). Make the best five-card hand from your two cards and the five on the table.\n\nBetting happens before the flop and after each new card. Fold to give up the hand, check if nobody has bet, call to match a bet, or bet and raise to put more in. All in means pushing every chip you have. A raise must be at least as big as the last one.\n\nIf you cannot match a bet you can still go all in. Extra chips go into a side pot that only the players who matched it can win. When the betting ends, the best hand wins the pot, and equal hands split it.\n\nThe small and big blinds are forced bets that move around the table with the dealer button. They can rise as the game goes on, so a game always ends.\n\nUse Hint for your odds and a suggestion. Undo takes back your last bet before the next card is dealt (not in online games).</string>
